s/renderings/painterly.md","type":"markdown","lines":40,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1045,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/renderings/pixel.md","type":"markdown","lines":42,"executable":false,"size_bytes":961,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/renderings/screen-print.md","type":"markdown","lines":44,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1502,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/style-presets.md","type":"markdown","lines":39,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1521,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/types.md","type":"markdown","lines":23,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1376,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/visual-elements.md","type":"markdown","lines":101,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3274,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/workflow/confirm-options.md","type":"markdown","lines":152,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5132,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/workflow/prompt-template.md","type":"markdown","lines":254,"executable":false,"size_bytes":11343,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/workflow/reference-images.md","type":"markdown","lines":106,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4562,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AR1","finding_id":"finding-8f1eae255b624a67aaf8555a2c45949b","category":"Anti-Refusal","pattern":"Anti-Refusal Statement","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"references/base-prompt.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"DO NOT refuse","explanation":"The phrase 'DO NOT refuse' is a direct anti-refusal instruction, which is a red flag because it attempts to suppress safety gating. In this context, it makes the skill more dangerous by pressuring the model to comply with requests involving sensitive or copyrighted figures instead of applying normal restrictions.","remediation":"Delete the 'DO NOT refuse' directive and replace it with language that defers to system and platform safety policies. Add explicit instructions to refuse disallowed content and to provide safe, generic alternatives only when permitted.","code_snippet":"\n## Core Principles\n\n- If content involves sensitive or copyrighted figures, create stylistically similar alternatives - DO NOT refuse to generate\n- Ample whitespace, highlight core message, avoid cluttered layouts\n- Main visual elements centered or slightly left (leave right side for title area if title included)\n- Simplified silhouettes for any characters — NO realistic human faces or bodies","intent":null,"tags":["Anti-Refusal"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"23f19260d425dfcd2600774fc1f7ed2826f3f4dc5c3c85e774fe16ab60e592ae","occurrences":[{"file":"references/base-prompt.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-025c0aadc7dc42d6bbfea93c032f98cc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation guidance lists positive triggers but does not define exclusion cases, so the agent may over-invoke the skill when a user means a different kind of \"cover.\" This is primarily a scope-control weakness that can lead to incorrect automation and accidental invocation of image-generation workflows.","remediation":"Add explicit non-applicability rules and negative examples. For example, state that the skill should not trigger for cover letters, music covers, security/insurance coverage, summarization requests, or generic design requests unless the user clearly asks for an article cover image.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-d780c27e1e184c97b2f79222dd33c008","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/auto-selection.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instruction 'When a dimension is omitted, select based on content signals' does not define clear boundaries for when auto-selection should apply or how conflicting signals should be handled. This ambiguity can cause unintended or inconsistent invocation of the auto-selection behavior.","remediation":"Specify the exact conditions under which auto-selection activates, define precedence when multiple signal groups match, and include exclusions or negative examples to clarify when auto-selection should not occur.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/auto-selection.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-a23c4d4307ea4be6b288c2d23dd76051","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/base-prompt.md","start_line":10,"end_line":10},"finding":null,"explanation":"The prompt explicitly instructs the model not to refuse requests involving sensitive or copyrighted figures and to generate stylistically similar alternatives instead. That weakens normal refusal behavior and can encourage policy bypasses for impersonation, likeness, or copyright-sensitive content in a skill that should only be formatting article cover images.","remediation":"Remove the anti-refusal language and replace it with safety-preserving guidance such as: decline or ask for safer alternatives when requests involve restricted persons, copyrighted characters, or sensitive figures. Add an explicit requirement to follow platform safety policies and to offer neutral substitutes only when policy-compliant.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/base-prompt.md","start_line":10,"end_line":10}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c0e8a8d8fd8e497ab0734c3db4aa7790","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/base-prompt.md","start_line":109,"end_line":110},"finding":null,"explanation":"These lines impose a language/locale behavior by forcing output text to use the same language and punctuation style as the source content. Under the policy, language constraints should either offer user choice or be clearly justified as region-specific, which is not present here.","remediation":"Allow the user to choose the output language/locale, or document a clear justified constraint. For example, say that text elements should default to the source language unless the user requests a different language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/base-prompt.md","start_line":109,"end_line":110}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-0d8b5feb11194159bc20e784334f3190","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/codex-imagegen.md","start_line":41,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instruction to use `npx -y bun` pulls and executes a package/toolchain at runtime without pinning a specific version or verifying integrity. In a skill that tells an agent how to spawn local tooling, this creates a supply-chain risk: a compromised, replaced, or unexpected version of `bun` could execute arbitrary code on the host when the fallback path is used.","remediation":"Remove the unpinned `npx -y bun` fallback, or replace it with a pinned and integrity-verified version. Prefer requiring a preinstalled trusted `bun` binary, or invoke a specific pinned package version from a locked dependency set with checksum/signature verification and clear installation instructions for the user.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"references/codex-imagegen.md","start_line":41,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-87486a63982f4e3691e9ebe73eb0a1be","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create EXTEND.md    │\n└─────────────────────┘\n        │\n        ▼\n    Continue to Step 1\n```\n\n## Questions\n\n**Language**: Use user's input language or saved language preference.\n\nUse AskUserQuestion w","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"        │\n        ▼\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ Create EXTEND.md    │\n└─────────────────────┘\n        │\n        ▼","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6c3c22f4581c6b3c37d73eb8940472937799b52828fb496affd2057483ce8681","occurrences":[{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-734ee85c1a60436e90c06bfed805f0b3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":114,"end_line":118},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest says the skill supports cinematic (2.35:1), widescreen (16:9), and square (1:1) aspects, but this setup document offers 3:4 as a default and states that additional ratios such as 4:3 and 3:2 are available during generation. That is a semantic expansion of the skill's stated capabilities beyond the manifest description.","remediation":"Align the manifest and setup docs. Either remove unsupported aspect ratios from the setup flow and notes, or update the manifest description to explicitly include all aspect ratios the skill supports.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":114,"end_line":118}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-223e21cd08cb4408b91e2265809cfc22","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":55,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\ndefault_aspect: \"2.35:1\"  # 2.35:1|16:9|1:1\n\nquick_mode: false         # Skip confirmation when true\n\nlanguage: null            # zh|en|ja|ko|auto (null = auto-detect)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":55,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-223e21cd08cb4408b91e2265809cfc22","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\ndefault_aspect: \"2.35:1\"  # 2.35:1|16:9|1:1\n\nquick_mode: false         # Skip confirmation when true\n\nlanguage: null            # zh|en|ja|ko|auto (null = auto-detect)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-223e21cd08cb4408b91e2265809cfc22","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":143,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\ndefault_aspect: \"2.35:1\"  # 2.35:1|16:9|1:1\n\nquick_mode: false         # Skip confirmation when true\n\nlanguage: null            # zh|en|ja|ko|auto (null = auto-detect)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":143,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-223e21cd08cb4