en|ja|ko|auto (null = auto-detect)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bf8f91dea4c54033bb1600e6d8fd224a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":31,"end_line":31},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a behavior that suppresses a confirmation step using only the terse note 'Skip confirmation when true'. Because confirmations are a safety control for actions that may affect user data or system behavior, the description should explicitly warn users about the consequences of enabling this mode.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the `quick_mode` field and examples stating that enabling it bypasses confirmation safeguards and should only be used when the user is comfortable with unattended or less-reviewed operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":31,"end_line":31}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-4a07e9c12ad641578db12527f404aab8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/workflow/confirm-options.md","start_line":36,"end_line":36},"finding":null,"explanation":"Line L036 states that language is auto-determined and that there is 'No need to ask,' which imposes a language/locale decision without explicit user opt-in. This matches the policy category for language or locale constraints that do not offer the user a choice.","remediation":"Allow the user to confirm or override the detected language, or document this as an explicit opt-in preference. For example, present the detected language as the default while providing a clear way to switch languages.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/workflow/confirm-options.md","start_line":36,"end_line":36}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-83fe6406d7a647dda9c21914dab0b712","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation guidance lists positive triggers but does not define exclusion cases, so the agent may over-invoke the skill when a user means a different kind of \"cover.\" This is primarily a scope-control weakness that can lead to incorrect automation and accidental invocation of image-generation workflows.","remediation":"Add explicit non-applicability rules and negative examples. For example, state that the skill should not trigger for cover letters, music covers, security/insurance coverage, summarization requests, or generic design requests unless the user clearly asks for an article cover image.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-87158871857948f3aacf93aaff831306","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":191,"end_line":191},"finding":null,"explanation":"This natural-language instruction hard-requires a specific tool name despite earlier text saying such names are examples and local equivalents should be substituted. That creates an avoidable runtime-policy mismatch by prescribing one interface rather than offering user- or runtime-dependent choice.","remediation":"Rewrite the instruction to require an interactive user-input tool generically, e.g. \"Use the runtime's available interactive user-input tool (such as `AskUserQuestion` or equivalent)\" instead of m